---
import Chapter from '../Chapter.astro';
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';
import FigBuildValidate from '../figures/FigBuildValidate.astro';

const questions = [
  {
    when: 'Before issuing',
    q: 'What does a cross-certificate enable before it is signed?',
    now: 'Constraints are audited afterwards, with the bridge already in production.',
  },
  {
    when: 'During the handshake',
    q: 'Which admissible path does the receiver prefer, under its own policy?',
    now: 'The vendor of each validation library decides, the same way for everyone.',
  },
  {
    when: 'After the decision',
    q: 'Why was a path accepted, or why was there none?',
    now: 'A trust store says yes or no. Nothing records the reason.',
  },
];
---

<Chapter id="gap" num="03" kicker="The gap" title="Validating a path is specified. Choosing it is not.">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      RFC 5280 validates a chain in detail, but its first input is literally <em
        >"a prospective certification path"</em
      >: it does not search for one, and it does not prefer one. RFC 4158 describes how to build
      paths and is only informational. SCVP lets a client ask a server for the best path and <strong
        >never defines what makes a path better</strong
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      Meanwhile, constraints such as <code>nameConstraints</code> or <code>pathLenConstraint</code> are
      only checked once a chain has been walked, so path builders explore branches that were condemned
      before the walk started.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure num={3} caption="Building and validating are specified by different documents, and nothing in between says which path to choose.">
    <FigBuildValidate />
  </Figure>

  <p class="key">Nobody knows what a cross-certificate enables before it is issued.</p>

  <div class="questions grid-3">
    {
      questions.map((x, i) => (
        <div class="rule-top">
          <p class="label">
            {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')} · {x.when}
          </p>
          <h3>{x.q}</h3>
          <p class="small">{x.now}</p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</Chapter>

<style>
  .questions {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .questions .label {
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
  }
  .questions h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
  .questions .small {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
